HST Office: the Header & Footer tab of Writer's ribbon follows the cursor into a header or footer.

vcl gets the context HeaderFooter (`context-HeaderFooter` in a notebookbar .ui). The cursor in a header
or footer leaves the shell's context at Text (or Table), so the sidebar keeps its decks; instead
SwView::SelectShell tells the Tabbed notebookbar of the frame (hst::ribbon::SetRibbonSubContext). The
tab control then shows the pages of that context beside those of the current context and opens the
first of them, as Office opens Header & Footer when a header is entered; leaving it hides them and goes
back to the default tab when one of them was current. A change of the selection's context while in the
header keeps the current Header & Footer tab. Nothing changes when no page has the context.

- include/vcl/EnumContext.hxx, vcl/source/window/EnumContext.cxx: Context::HeaderFooter.
- include/vcl/HstRibbonContext.hxx (new), include/vcl/tabctrl.hxx, vcl/source/control/tabctrl.cxx.
- sw/source/uibase/uiview/view.cxx.

